				\begin{document}$$\begin{aligned} \begin{aligned} F^{k}_{1-\frac{1}{2},j}&:= 0, \quad F^{k}_{{\mathcal {N}}+\frac{1}{2},j}:= 0, \quad j = 1, \dots , {\mathcal {N}},\\ F^{k}_{i,1-\frac{1}{2}}&:= 0, \quad F^{k}_{i,{\mathcal {N}}+\frac{1}{2}}:= 0, \quad i = 1, \dots , {\mathcal {N}}. \end{aligned} \end{aligned}$$\end{document}F1-12,jk:=0,FN+12,jk:=0,j=1,⋯,N,Fi,1-12k:=0,Fi,N+12k:=0,i=1,⋯,N.Notice that we employ a fully explicit scheme to avoid Newton sub-iterations that could be computationally expensive. Computational times of simulations could be reduced by using more efficient numerical schemes, such as implicit-explicit schemes whereby diffusion terms are discretised implicitly but all other terms are discretised explicitly (Hundsdorfer et al. 2003).
